WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:07.080
All the world's a stage and all the blah,
blah, blah.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:12.260
We all know how that one goes. But if you are
a theatrical type, there's a good chance you

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.930
became smitten at a very young age.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:24.890
The sweetest sounds I ever hear are still
inside my head.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:30.500
Seeing the wonders of a life you might be
part of one day. Full of stories and

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:37.580
experiences you can only dream about from
the eighth row, behind two beehives in row seven.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:48.230
The most entrancing sight of all is yet for me to see.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:52.480
And the dearest love in all

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:59.490
the world is waiting somewhere for me.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:03.750
Is waiting somewhere.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:08.910
Somewhere for me.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:27.690
Once smitten, though, then comes the work of
classes and training, of speech and technique.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:33.120
Honing your craft as you pound the
pavement in New York City, auditioning for

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:38.460
anything and everything, all in pursuit of
that moment in the spotlight where you hope

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:46.740
someone might see you, really see you and say
those magic words, "Where have you been?"

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:57.820
But what if those magic words never come? And
it's only rejection over and over again, year

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.310
after year, and near miss

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:01.920
after near miss.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:06.580
Until you realize that near miss has become
your life.

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:11.150
How do you keep at it with any hope?

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:21.840
Thank you. Very nice. So, someone's shown up
who's not on our list.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.950
Maybe a walk-in? I do know her.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:30.120
She's capable, a little vanilla, but we've
got about ten minutes until lunch.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.080
Yeah, sure.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.290
Loretta Durkin, you still there?

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:34.300
Yes!

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:37.650
Yes. Hi.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:43.650
Oh, hi. I'm so sorry. I thought- my agent
assured me that I was on the list.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.500
And do you have the pages for the role of the
nanny?

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.160
Yes. Is it just the one scene?

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.050
That's right. Whenever you're ready.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.260
Enough. Enough of your questions, Detective.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:11.120
I'm happy to tell you who I am and what it is
I do without your insistent probing.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.530
I am a caretaker of children to whom I'm given
charge.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:19.820
Am I a substitute for the child's true
mother?

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:27.040
Some would prefer I say 'no', but I believe I
am.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.570
I must be.

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:38.400
Their mother when it's only me with them.
Because a child needs to feel at all times

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:45.420
safe. They need to feel protected with the
kind of ferocity only a mother can summon.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:53.470
It's no matter if they were born of my own
flesh.

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:03.340
Would I kill to protect a child in my charge?

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:13.990
That is the question you have for me, I
assume, Detective. To that, I would say

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:19.390
without so much as blinking, I would kill
without compunction.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:31.140
But the sake and safety of any child in my
care. So.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:34.300
Now you have your answer.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:38.770
Where have you been?

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:44.680
Um-

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:50.040
But when you finally do land your dream,
your moment in that spotlight...

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:52.090
I said, Where have you been?

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.120
Oh.

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:58.880
How far would you go to hang onto it?

00:04:58.970 --> 00:04:59.410
Oh.

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:04.190
Oh, thank you. Oh, thank you.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:05.600
Oh, God.

